      "explanation": {
        "category": "complete_confounding",
        "kind": "refusal",
        "status": "written",
        "text": "Every unit given one treatment level also shares a recorded nuisance level, such as a chamber, with no unit of the other treatment level; for example, all runs of one recipe were in one chamber and all runs of the other recipe in another. A treatment difference and a chamber difference would then produce exactly the same data, so no analysis can separate them. (For a numbered factor such as run order, the same happens when the treatment lines up exactly with a straight-line trend in it.) Measuring more wafers or sites does not help, because it adds no comparison of the treatments within a chamber. The design has to change so that every treatment level runs at every level of that factor, as in the reassignment suggestion when one is given.",
